# Settings a platform release introduces that a deployment's .env must gain when it updates.
#
# One line per setting: since|KEY|value|comment. `since` is the platform version that introduced the setting,
# `value` is what update.sh appends when .env lacks the key and the deployment is on an older release, and the
# comment is written above it. A project or plugin declares its own in an env-additions file at its root, which
# the packager merges with this one. Declare a setting here only when its absence would stop the release from
# booting or leave it wrong in a way a later edit cannot repair, and only with a value every deployment can take;
# a value that needs a judgement belongs in the release notes. An entry stays here once released: a deployment that
# skips releases needs every entry introduced after its own version. scripts/lib/release_sign.py validates the file
# and names the keys an update never writes.
